Package: spatialert
Title: Interactive Spatial Hotspot Analysis for Public Health
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Emily A.", "Serman", email = "eserman@clemson.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Brian", "Witrick", role = "aut"),
    person("Lior", "Rennert", role = "aut"))
Description: A Shiny-based tool for identifying and visualizing spatial hotspots
    in public health data using the Getis-Ord Gi* statistic. Designed for public
    health practitioners, spatialert runs entirely on the local machine so that
    sensitive data never leaves the user's environment. Supports school-level,
    facility-level, and pre-aggregated areal data at the county, census tract,
    or block group level for any US state.
